From 85035b802df7fa4ccc58dd639c8699be5d9b3378 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:10:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Open an installed Qaaf with no signal: a service worker
 (P-111, R6)

Chrome offers to install the web app, and the installed icon then opened
the browser's offline page: no service worker, so a lesson reloaded with
no signal, or the app opened on a train, showed the dinosaur (design
review, 24 and 28 October; launch bar R6).

web:meta now writes dist/sw.js and registers it, on export only, never
under expo start. The worker keeps what a first lesson needs: the app
shell, its CSS and JS, the seven fonts, the five reward sounds and the
two scenery images, each named from the build (20 files, 2,080 KB
gzipped, 5,736 KB raw; budget 2.5 MB and 6 MB). Pages go network first
and fall back to the kept shell; hashed files (name.<hash>.ext, and the
bundles' name-<hash>.js|css) are cache first; voice clips are kept as
they are played, at most 300. Its version is a hash of the kept files,
so a deploy that changes them replaces it, and it deletes only this
app's own qaaf- caches, since Cache Storage is shared with every
repository on the host. scripts/sw-kill.js is the off switch, to ship as
sw.js if the worker ever misbehaves.

One case is not covered: Home's address is the base without its slash
(/Urdu), written by the router after load, which lies outside the
worker's scope (/Urdu/), so reloading Home in a browser tab offline still
fails. An installed app launches at /Urdu/, inside it.

check:offline installs it in a real browser profile, cuts the network,
reloads l-1 (its first card, Nastaliq drawn) and opens the start address
(Home). Broken on purpose: with no registration it fails ("no service
worker installed"); with bundles left uncached (a dot-only hash
pattern, the first version's bug) it fails on both pages.

Design's specification, three viewpoints and the case against (a worker
outlives deploys and can strand a learner) are in tonight's report; the
second check is a different agent's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FgFsmHsJ32w9Di1MVKqKTX
